s a condition with well-documented clinical symptoms. These include 向心性肥胖 (central obesity), 满月脸 (moon face), 水牛背 (buffalo hump), and 肾上腺轴抑制 (HPA axis suppression). Case reports describe patients developing full Cushingoid features after using inhaled corticosteroids in combination with CYP3A4 inhibitors like ritonavir or clarithromycin, which increase systemic corticosteroid exposure [Data: Entities (15915, 17924, 18214, 18193, 18385); Relationships (17996, 17999, 9450, 9449)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Drug interactions significantly elevate risk of corticosteroid toxicity\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The risk of systemic corticosteroid effects from 丙酸氟替卡松吸入气雾剂 is markedly increased when co-administered with strong CYP3A4 inhibitors such as ritonavir. Evidence shows that ritonavir can substantially increase fluticasone propionate plasma concentrations, leading to markedly reduced serum cortisol levels and clinical manifestations of Cushing’s syndrome. This pharmacokinetic interaction is a critical safety concern, especially in patients with HIV or those receiving antiviral therapies containing protease inhibitors [Data: Relationships (290, 15092); Entities (14062, 11524)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"糖皮质激素类药物 as a class carry inherent risks of Cushing’s syndrome and adrenal suppression\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Beyond the specific drug 丙酸氟替卡松吸入气雾剂, the broader class of 糖皮质激素类药物 (glucocorticoid drugs) is associated with increased risk of Cushing’s syndrome and adrenal suppression, particularly when used concomitantly with CYP3A4 inhibitors like nirmatrelvir/ritonavir. Although short treatment duration may lower overall risk, the potential for clinically significant drug-drug interactions remains, warranting careful monitoring in vulnerable populations such as pediatric patients [Data: Entities (11524); Relationships (15092)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Clinical indicators like serum cortisol help detect systemic corticosteroid effects\",\n            \"explanation\": \"血清皮质醇浓度 (serum cortisol concentration) serves as a key biomarker for assessing HPA axis function and detecting systemic corticosteroid exposure. In cases involving 丙酸氟替卡松吸入气雾剂 combined with ritonavir, marked reductions in serum cortisol have been observed, confirming significant adrenal suppression. Monitoring this indicator is essential for early detection of iatrogenic Cushing’s syndrome or adrenal insufficiency in at-risk patients [Data: Entities (14062); Relationships (290)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"皮质类固醇过量 leads to库欣综合征表现\",\n            \"explanation\": \"皮质类固醇过量 (corticosteroid excess) is causally linked to 库欣综合征表现 (Cushingoid manifestations), as noted in literature discussing drug interactions involving inhaled corticosteroids and CYP3A4 inhibitors. Strong inhibitors like ritonavir or itraconazole can lead to accumulation of corticosteroids, resulting in clinical signs consistent with Cushing’s syndrome. This underscores the importance of recognizing drug interaction risks even with inhaled formulations [Data: Entities (16596, 18046); Relationships (18353)].\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is high due to the potential for serious, systemic adverse effects—including life-altering endocrine and metabolic disturbances—from a commonly used inhaled medication when combined with widely prescribed drugs like antivirals or antibiotics.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782127005, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1340, "prompt_tokens": 4621, "total_tokens": 5961, "completion_to